-- title:
--   Corollary 12 — the relation generated by a hyperfinite R and an R-compatible countable-to-one map is hyperfinite
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $X$ is a standard Borel space, $\mu$ a $\sigma$-finite measure on $X$, and $R \subseteq X \times X$ a discrete measured equivalence relation for $\mu$ (`IsDiscreteMeasured`): a Borel equivalence relation whose classes are countable and for which $\mu$ is quasi-invariant (the saturation of a null Borel set is null).
--
--   Suppose $R$ is hyperfinite, and let $\theta : X \to X$ be non-singular (`IsNonsingular`: measurable, and $\mu(\theta^{-1}A) = 0$ exactly when $\mu(A) = 0$), countable-to-one (every fibre $\theta^{-1}\{x\}$ is countable), and compatible with $R$ ($x \sim_R y$ implies $\theta(x) \sim_R \theta(y)$). Then the relation $R_\theta$, in which $(y, x) \in R_\theta$ exactly when $\theta^n(x) \sim_R \theta^m(y)$ for some $n, m \in \mathbb N$, is hyperfinite (`IsHyperfinite`): off some $\mu$-null Borel set, $R_\theta$ is a discrete measured equivalence relation and an increasing union of type I relations. “Non-singular” has its usual meaning; how far “up to a null set” reaches is set out with the definition of hyperfinite in the definitions bundle.
-- source:
--   Connes, A., Feldman, J., Weiss, B., An amenable equivalence relation is generated by a single transformation, Ergodic Theory Dynam. Systems 1 (1981) 431–450, https://doi.org/10.1017/S014338570000136X, pp. 444–445, Corollary 12

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConnesFeldmanWeiss

namespace ConnesFeldmanWeiss

theorem isHyperfinite_tailRel_of_isHyperfinite {X : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X]
    [StandardBorelSpace X] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure X) [MeasureTheory.SigmaFinite μ]
    (R : Set (X × X)) (hR : IsDiscreteMeasured μ R) (hhyp : IsHyperfinite μ R)
    (θ : X → X) (hθ : IsNonsingular μ θ) (hcount : ∀ x, (θ ⁻¹' {x}).Countable)
    (hresp : ∀ x y, (x, y) ∈ R → (θ x, θ y) ∈ R) :
    IsHyperfinite μ {p : X × X | ∃ n m : ℕ, (θ^[n] p.2, θ^[m] p.1) ∈ R} := by
  sorry

end ConnesFeldmanWeiss
